WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to show another --
Yeah, you were posting

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of old photos.
This is you

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:05.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that's Simon Rich
and that's Marika Sawyer.

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:09.776
And the three of you wrote
together and dear friends.

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:12.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, we wrote
about three sketches together

00:00:12.445 --> 00:00:13.747 line:92%
every week for three years.

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:15.715 line:92%
We were the closest of friends.

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.017 line:92%
And, uh, we would all sit --

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:18.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
The three of us would sit
in a room

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:20.620 align:start size:94% position:6%
writing filthy sketches
all night long.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you would kind of check in
and be like,

00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:23.256 line:92%
"What are you guys doing?"

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:24.357 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And you'd get a piece of it

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
and be like,
"No, I don't like it."

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:26.493 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:29.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, uh, so we were doing
a Thanksgiving scene,

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:31.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we thought,
"Let's take a picture,

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:34.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we'll make a Thanksgiving
card for Seth.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.068 line:92%
And, uh, we'll give it to him."

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:38.304
So, that was the photo we took,
and, uh, we made a card,

00:00:38.304 --> 00:00:39.606 line:92%
and it had this on the front.

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:42.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
It said,
"Happy Thanksgiving, Seth."

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:43.109 line:92%
And then, when you opened it,

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
it said,
"We [bleep] each other."

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:45.345 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:49.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
And...then we signed it.
It was nice.

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:49.983 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:51.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was nice.
-Yeah.

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:55.221
-Um, we -- Another "SNL" sketch
you were in

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:57.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
is a writer we both love
wrote --

00:00:57.891 --> 00:00:58.691 size:81% position:41% line:92%
This is "Drag Brunch."

00:00:58.691 --> 00:00:59.959 line:92%
-Thrill of a lifetime. Yes.

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:00.660 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-James Anderson --

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:01.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
How would you describe
James Anderson,

00:01:01.761 --> 00:01:03.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
for those who aren't
lucky enough to know him?

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:06.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Don't be distracted
by this photo.

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:09.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
James Anderson is the writer
who wrote this sketch,

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:12.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Drag Brunch," and is the
funniest person in the world

00:01:12.906 --> 00:01:14.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that any of us
have ever worked with.

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:16.843
-Absolutely consistently funny,
week after week.

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:18.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's been working at "SNL"
since, I think, 2000.

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:21.414 size:78% position:39%
-Yes. And would come
into the rewrite room

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:23.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
not knowing
what anyone was pitching on

00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:26.986
and pitch a joke that would
work better than anything.

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:27.987 line:92%
He would walk in and say like,

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Why doesn't she just go,
'I want a Purpsi'?"

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:31.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we'd be like, "All right.
We'll put that in."

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:35.595 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, just, like, funny bones,
funny bones.

00:01:35.595 --> 00:01:37.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, uh, he wrote a sketch
called "Drag Brunch,"

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:40.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I said to him,
"It is the thrill of my life

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be in a sketch
that you wrote."

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:42.502 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-And it was fantastic.

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:43.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I got
to wear heels on concrete,

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is fun.
-Did it -- Did you --

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:47.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do your shins still hurt
from wearing --

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:49.309 line:92%
-No, we figured it out good.

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:52.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
Uh, me and the wonderful
costume department --

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:53.213 line:92%
You know, we judged based --

00:01:53.213 --> 00:01:56.916
I have a tear in my hip, too,
so we were factoring that in.

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:59.219 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Got it.
-How high the heels could be.

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:02.388 align:start size:94% position:6%
Walking on concrete,
never having done it before.

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:04.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
Super nervous.
All those things went in.

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:07.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
We went with a low heel.
-Oh, wow.

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:09.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you have
a greater appreciation

00:02:09.329 --> 00:02:11.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
for those in drag
for how hard it was?

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:14.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Um, I have a greater
appreciation for those shoes

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:15.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
and for all the times
I've been like,

00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:17.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Come on! Let's get the cab!"
You know?

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:21.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Come on! The Uber's here!

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:22.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
-I like --

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:24.277 line:92%
Watch me walk in real time.

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.346 line:92%
It's like -- It was like...

00:02:26.346 --> 00:02:29.415 line:92%
when a -- when a cow's born.

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:30.183 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:32.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
A calf, I guess you'd say.
-They're called calves.

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:34.687 line:92%
-They're called calves at first.

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.756 line:92%
-This is a sketch you wrote.

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:38.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
You and Colin Jost
wrote this years ago.

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:41.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. And you didn't pick it.
-Uh...

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:43.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
I --
-You were the head of writing.

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:45.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was the head of writing,
but I thought --

00:02:45.265 --> 00:02:46.032 line:92%
I remember saying, like --

00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:48.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm like, "Save it
for when he comes back."

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:48.735 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.735 --> 00:02:50.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"I'll wait
till one of these writers

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:52.539 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
improbably hosts."

00:02:52.539 --> 00:02:56.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You were a "Les Mis" fan
as a child.

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:57.544 line:92%
So this -- I should point out,

00:02:57.544 --> 00:02:59.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
this sketch was called
"Diner Lobster."

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:00.513 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:02.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it was to
the "Les Mis" soundtrack.

00:03:02.649 --> 00:03:06.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, it was about
a diner that serves lobster,

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:07.120 size:84% position:42% line:92%
as some in New York do.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:09.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
Someone finally
orders the lobster,

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:10.223 line:92%
and we bring out the lobster,

00:03:10.223 --> 00:03:13.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
who's Kenan playing
a Jean Valjean type.

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:15.128 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He's facing death.

00:03:15.128 --> 00:03:16.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's lived in the diner
for 40 years,

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:21.701
and the only music to accompany
that is "Les Miserables."

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.469 line:92%
So what we did was we wrote it

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:25.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
by listening
to the "Les Mis" soundtrack,

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:27.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then we changed
the words of the songs

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:30.577 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we made them
about being a lobster.

00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:31.978 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:32.946 line:92%
-And that's sketch writing.

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:36.549 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And that was at the table
in 2010.

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:36.983 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:38.685 line:92%
-And I remember it was done.

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:40.019 line:92%
And it wasn't like you were mad,

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:41.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
but everyone was just like,
"Guys."

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:45.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And then we moved on.

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:46.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now it's on TV.
-Who'd you write it for?

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:48.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you remember who
you originally wrote it for?

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:51.164 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Um, I think Galifianakis
was the host.

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:51.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, all right.
-Yeah.

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:57.604
-Well, I think you elevated it.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.604 --> 00:04:01.140 size:81% position:41%
There's a person on TV
you get mistaken for.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:01.574 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes.

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:03.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you got mistaken
in the park the other day?

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:04.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, this has been
happening a lot.

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:08.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not saying
I look like The Flash, but...

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:09.315 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh!

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:11.517
-I've been told enough --
-Somebody just went "Oh"

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:12.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
like they kind of see it.
-Oh.

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:14.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're like --
Now they think I'm The Flash.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's happened enough
that I need to say something.

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.359 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm not The Flash.

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:20.326 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.326 --> 00:04:21.027 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I was at the dog park.

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:22.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had my dog. Don't worry.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.195 --> 00:04:28.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I see this woman --
older woman and a little boy

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:30.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
are walking along
the gate of the dog park,

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:32.572
and the boy is jumping up
to look over the gate.

00:04:32.572 --> 00:04:37.677
And he's jumping up and he goes,
"Flash. Flash. Flash."

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:41.314
Like he had a little accent from
like, old Europe when old --

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:43.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
like old spelled with an E,
you know?

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:46.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Like, "Flash, Flash!"

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:50.423
And his companion, grandmother,
whatever, she goes,

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:52.091 line:92%
"He says you are The Flash."

00:04:52.091 --> 00:04:54.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said,
"No, I'm not The Flash."

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:57.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, and he keeps going,
"Flash, Flash."

00:04:57.730 --> 00:05:01.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she goes, "Are you sure
you're not The Flash?"

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "It happens
from time to time.

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:04.337 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm not The Flash."

00:05:04.337 --> 00:05:06.139
Right at that second, someone
walked up who recognized me

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:08.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
from stand-up comedy and said,
"Hey, I'm a big fan."

00:05:08.608 --> 00:05:10.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I went,
"Thank you very much."

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:11.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they walked away.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:17.317
And then I locked eyes with the
grandmother and she was so mad.

00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:19.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she looked at me
and she said,

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:22.522 line:92%
"No, you are not The Flash."

00:05:22.522 --> 00:05:23.056 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.056 --> 00:05:26.426
-Just for those who don't know,
let's go over to camera one.

00:05:26.426 --> 00:05:28.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's the Flash.
-Yeah, it's not --

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:31.197 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not perfect.
-It's not bad, though.

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:33.566
-When I came home -- I came back
to the apartment,

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:35.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"I'm sick of being The Flash!"

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:38.271 align:start size:94% position:6%
I gave no context to my wife,
no context.

00:05:38.271 --> 00:05:38.805 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.805 --> 00:05:40.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, "This kid thinks
I was The Flash.

00:05:40.606 --> 00:05:41.507 line:92%
And the grandma's mad at me.

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:44.277
and then, this guy said
he was a big fan of mine,

00:05:44.277 --> 00:05:45.078 line:92%
and that was embarrassing."

00:05:45.078 --> 00:05:47.680
And my wife, Anna, was like,
"So, let me get this straight.

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:51.584
Your two problems are that
a fan said he likes your work

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:54.520 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that people think you look
like a 25-year-old,

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:58.491
handsome actor who, by the way,
you don't look like."

00:05:58.491 --> 00:06:01.427 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

